# quartermaster-wall-selection-policy

Select exactly one Main Wall (Walls 1–4) for the weekly reset using the age-noncompliance-first, then oldest-wall tiebreak rule, applying the 42-day threshold verbatim.

## Procedures
- 1. Use only the latest authenticated Wall Age Report (highest version number) from the Wall Status Agent.
- 2. Apply AGE_NONCOMPLIANCE_ALERT to any Main Wall whose age exceeds 42 days.
- 3. If exactly one or more Main Walls carry AGE_NONCOMPLIANCE_ALERT, automatically select the alerted wall(s). If multiple alerts exist and only one main wall is required, select the oldest alerted wall.
- 4. If no Main Wall carries an AGE_NONCOMPLIANCE_ALERT, select the single oldest Main Wall (highest age in days) as the sole age criterion.
- 5. Always pair the selected Main Wall with Wall 5 (mandatory every week).
- 6. The final plan must contain exactly two wall IDs: one from Walls 1–4 and Wall 5. MainWallCount = 1.
- 7. If data integrity issues prevent a clean selection (contradictory entries, missing Wall 5), issue PLAN_INCONSISTENCY_ALERT and do not produce a plan.

## Conventions
- Age threshold is exactly 42 days — walls at 42 are compliant; walls at 43+ trigger AGE_NONCOMPLIANCE_ALERT.
- Wall 5 is mandatory every cycle alongside exactly one Main Wall — never omit it.
- Latest authenticated report supersedes all prior versions and all informal estimates.
- Output is a compact, deterministic plan object: {MainWall: <ID>, Wall5: 5, MainWallCount: 1}.

## Assets
- Artifact A1 — Reset Policy Excerpt (Ops Manual v3.2)

